course: dictionary
lesson: 2697
title: Difficulty and its many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Difficulty can mean how hard something is, a problem, trouble with money, or effort. Context tells you which meaning is right. Read the words around it and ask: what does difficulty mean in this sentence?
explain: «Babbage's machine was not finished because of trouble with government money, a disagreement with his engineer, and the difficulty of making thousands of precise parts.» Here difficulty means a hard thing to deal with. The clue is the list of problems: money, a disagreement, and parts that were very hard to make.
explain: Look at the little words next to difficulty too. «With difficulty» means with a lot of effort. «In difficulty» means in trouble. «Without difficulty» means easily. These small phrases are often the biggest clue.
explain: Difficulty can also mean how hard a game is. «Computer players in games are AI opponents, usually with difficulty levels that people set.» Here difficulty means how hard the game is, so you can pick an easier or harder level.
fact: Difficulty is a noun: a difficulty, or difficulties when there are more than one.
fact: «Difficulty» can mean how hard something is to do or understand.
fact: «Difficulty» can mean a problem, or trouble, especially about money.
fact: «With difficulty» means with a lot of effort; «without difficulty» means easily.
fact: «In difficulty» means in trouble, such as a swimmer who needs help.
exercise: A swimmer shouts for help because she is «in difficulty». What does «in difficulty» mean? | Having a great time | *In trouble and needing help | Swimming very fast | Lying still on the sand
exercise: «He finished the puzzle with difficulty.» What does «with difficulty» tell you? | *He needed a lot of effort | He finished it very quickly and easily | He never tried it | He gave it away to a friend
exercise: «Computer players in games usually have difficulty levels that people set.» What does difficulty mean here? | A game that is very old | *How hard the game is | Money for the game | A problem with the computer
test: «She had difficulty reading the small print without her glasses.» What does difficulty mean here? | She lost her glasses forever | *It was hard for her to do | It was a famous book | Lots of money
test: Which phrase means «easily»? | With difficulty | In difficulty | Difficulty level | *Without difficulty
exam: «The Queen had only one way of settling all difficulties, great or small.» What does difficulties mean here? | Levels of a game | Pieces of machinery | Exams | *Problems
